{"stage":"04_property_discovery","mock":false,"llm_call_executed":true,"source_scope":{"previous_spec_summary_available":true,"previous_code_summary_available":true,"provided_material_complete":true,"missing_or_unavailable_material":[]},"candidate_properties":[{"property_id":"P16_MLK_POLY_ADD_001","property_family_id":"P16","title":"In-place coefficient-wise addition preserves exact old-state/new-state relation under overflow-free assumptions","category":"polynomial_add_sub_bounds","verification_strategy":"standard_cbmc_harness","proof_obligation_kind":"functional","support_classification":"production_supported","required_tool_capabilities":["standard_cbmc_harness"],"candidate_statement":"For mlk_poly_add(mlk_poly *r, const mlk_poly *b), under the stated non-aliasing and overflow-preventing preconditions, each coefficient index k in [0, MLKEM_N) satisfies r->coeffs[k] == old(*r).coeffs[k] + b->coeffs[k] after the call, and only r->coeffs is modified.","supporting_evidence":[{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/poly.h","locator":"Declaration/comment and contract for mlk_poly_add","excerpt":"/* Add two polynomials in place. ... The coefficients of @p r and @p b must be such that the addition does not overflow. Otherwise, the behaviour of this function is undefined. ... @param[in,out] r Input-output polynomial to be added to. @param[in]     b Input polynomial that should be added to @p r. Must be disjoint from @p r. */ ... requires(memory_no_alias(r, sizeof(mlk_poly))) requires(memory_no_alias(b, sizeof(mlk_poly))) requires(forall(k0, 0, MLKEM_N, (int32_t) r->coeffs[k0] + b->coeffs[k0] <= INT16_MAX)) requires(forall(k1, 0, MLKEM_N, (int32_t) r->coeffs[k1] + b->coeffs[k1] >= INT16_MIN)) ensures(forall(k, 0, MLKEM_N, r->coeffs[k] == old(*r).coeffs[k] + b->coeffs[k])) assigns(memory_slice(r, sizeof(mlk_poly)))","supports_claim":"The header contract explicitly states in-place addition, disjoint inputs, overflow-preventing preconditions, the old/new-state relation, and the write footprint.","confidence":"high"},{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/poly.c","locator":"mlk_poly_add function body and loop invariants","excerpt":"for (i = 0; i < MLKEM_N; i++) __loop__( invariant(i <= MLKEM_N) invariant(forall(k0, i, MLKEM_N, r->coeffs[k0] == loop_entry(*r).coeffs[k0])) invariant(forall(k1, 0, i, r->coeffs[k1] == loop_entry(*r).coeffs[k1] + b->coeffs[k1])) decreases(MLKEM_N - i)) { /* The preconditions imply that the addition stays within int16_t. */ r->coeffs[i] = (int16_t)(r->coeffs[i] + b->coeffs[i]); }","supports_claim":"The body performs per-index signed addition in a single bounded loop and the loop invariants encode the prefix/suffix old-state/new-state split.","confidence":"high"},{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-agent-workflow-26-property-test/inputs/specs/fips203_clean.txt","locator":"Section 2.4.5 and Section 2.4.4","excerpt":"The algebraic operations of addition and scalar multiplication in R_q and T_q are done coordinate-wise... an element f of R_q ... represented in pseudocode by the array (f_0, ..., f_255) ∈ Z_q^256... the addition of two NTT representations in pseudocode is performed by a statement of the form ĥ ← f̂ + ĝ, where ĥ, f̂, ĝ ∈ Z_q^256 are coefficient arrays.","supports_claim":"The specification supports coefficient-wise array-based addition semantics for polynomial and NTT representations.","confidence":"high"}],"required_assumptions":["r and b point to distinct fresh mlk_poly objects as required by memory_no_alias.","For every k in [0, MLKEM_N), (int32_t) r->coeffs[k] + b->coeffs[k] is within the int16_t range; otherwise the function's behavior is undefined per the header comment.","The harness should snapshot old(*r) before the call and compare against post-state values after the call."],"cbmc_feasibility":"high","risk_level":"medium","expected_artifact_type":"CBMC harness with explicit pre-state snapshot and coefficient-wise postcondition assertions","out_of_scope_boundaries":["Do not claim modular reduction to canonical [0, q-1] output for this C routine; the source explicitly performs plain int16_t addition with no reduction.","Do not broaden this into whole-ML-KEM correctness or full FIPS compliance."],"uncertainty":"The FIPS text gives mathematical coordinate-wise modular semantics, but the implementation contract is intentionally narrower: overflow-free signed 16-bit in-place addition. The candidate property is therefore framed at the C-level contract, not as modular arithmetic correctness.","limitations":["CBMC can check the local contract and loop-related safety, but this does not prove the caller-side assumptions hold in all contexts.","The property is intentionally scoped to mlk_poly_add and does not generalize to other polynomial routines."]},{"property_id":"P16_MLK_POLY_ADD_002","property_family_id":"P16","title":"Non-aliasing and frame-condition preservation for mlk_poly_add","category":"pointer_validity_and_aliasing","verification_strategy":"standard_cbmc_harness","proof_obligation_kind":"frame","support_classification":"production_supported","required_tool_capabilities":["standard_cbmc_harness"],"candidate_statement":"mlk_poly_add requires that r and b are non-aliasing fresh objects, and it assigns only the storage of r; a candidate harness should therefore assume pointer disjointness and check that b remains unchanged while only r->coeffs[0..MLKEM_N-1] may be modified.","supporting_evidence":[{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/poly.h","locator":"mlk_poly_add contract and parameter docs","excerpt":"requires(memory_no_alias(r, sizeof(mlk_poly))) requires(memory_no_alias(b, sizeof(mlk_poly))) ... assigns(memory_slice(r, sizeof(mlk_poly))) ... @param[in] b Input polynomial that should be added to @p r. Must be disjoint from @p r.","supports_claim":"Explicit non-aliasing and frame-condition obligations for the function.","confidence":"high"},{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/cbmc.h","locator":"memory_no_alias and memory_slice macros","excerpt":"#define memory_no_alias(...) __CPROVER_is_fresh(__VA_ARGS__)
#define memory_slice(...) __CPROVER_object_upto(__VA_ARGS__)","supports_claim":"The macros encode the freshness/non-alias and write-footprint contract style used by the function.","confidence":"high"},{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/poly.c","locator":"mlk_poly_add body","excerpt":"r->coeffs[i] = (int16_t)(r->coeffs[i] + b->coeffs[i]);","supports_claim":"The body only writes through r, not b.","confidence":"high"}],"required_assumptions":["The harness must model r and b as separate valid mlk_poly objects.","If the proof is intended to include b-immutability, the harness must snapshot b before the call and compare it after the call."],"cbmc_feasibility":"high","risk_level":"low","expected_artifact_type":"CBMC harness with explicit aliasing assumptions and frame assertions","out_of_scope_boundaries":["Do not weaken the explicit disjointness requirement into a permissive aliasing model; the header states b must be disjoint from r.","Do not claim any stronger heap-separation property than what is needed for this function's local contract."],"uncertainty":"The contract is explicit, but the exact CBMC object model for memory_slice is still a tool-level detail; the functional intent is clear from the source macros.","limitations":["This is a local contract/frame property only; it does not imply broader memory-safety for callers or surrounding code.","CBMC freshness assumptions can overconstrain the harness if used outside the exact contract context."]},{"property_id":"P16_MLK_POLY_ADD_003","property_family_id":"P16","title":"Coefficient-array bounds safety over the full 256-iteration loop","category":"array_bounds","verification_strategy":"standard_cbmc_harness","proof_obligation_kind":"safety","support_classification":"production_supported","required_tool_capabilities":["standard_cbmc_harness"],"candidate_statement":"The loop in mlk_poly_add iterates i from 0 to MLKEM_N-1 with MLKEM_N = 256, so a candidate CBMC harness can check that r->coeffs[i] and b->coeffs[i] are always accessed within the declared coefficient array bounds for all iterations.","supporting_evidence":[{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/poly.c","locator":"mlk_poly_add loop header","excerpt":"for (i = 0; i < MLKEM_N; i++)","supports_claim":"The loop covers exactly the 256 coefficient indices in order.","confidence":"high"},{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/poly.h","locator":"mlk_poly typedef","excerpt":"typedef struct
