":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/poly.h","locator":"mlk_poly_add requires clauses and overflow warning","excerpt":"The coefficients of @p r and @p b must be such that the addition does not overflow. Otherwise, the behaviour of this function is undefined. ... requires(forall(k0, 0, MLKEM_N, (int32_t) r->coeffs[k0] + b->coeffs[k0] <= INT16_MAX)) requires(forall(k1, 0, MLKEM_N, (int32_t) r->coeffs[k1] + b->coeffs[k1] >= INT16_MIN))","supports_claim":"The function's contract explicitly encodes overflow-preventing bounds.","confidence":"high"},{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/poly.c","locator":"mlk_poly_add body comment","excerpt":"/* The preconditions imply that the addition stays within int16_t. */ r->coeffs[i] = (int16_t)(r->coeffs[i] + b->coeffs[i]);","supports_claim":"The implementation directly relies on the preconditions to avoid overflow in the signed 16-bit addition.","confidence":"high"}],"required_assumptions":["The harness must assert the contract preconditions exactly as written, or equivalent stronger assumptions.","The C model used by CBMC must reflect the usual signed-overflow semantics relevant to int16_t promotion and cast behavior.","The harness should not rely on any modulo-q normalization, because the function does not perform it."],"cbmc_feasibility":"high","risk_level":"medium","expected_artifact_type":"CBMC harness with explicit overflow-precondition assumptions and arithmetic assertions","out_of_scope_boundaries":["Do not claim canonical modular range [0, q-1] for mlk_poly_add output; that is a separate mathematical spec-level notion and not the implementation behavior here.","Do not promote this into a claim about absence of overflow in all callers without establishing caller-side preconditions."],"uncertainty":"The source is explicit about intended overflow-free semantics, but proving the property still depends on how CBMC models integer promotions and whether the harness encodes the preconditions precisely.","limitations":["This is an implementation-level signed overflow property, not a proof of ML-KEM correctness.","It is only valid under the explicit preconditions; it does not hold unconditionally."]},{"property_id":"P16_MLK_POLY_ADD_005","property_family_id":"P16","title":"Loop invariant preservation of prefix/suffix state split","category":"loop_contract","verification_strategy":"native_loop_contract","proof_obligation_kind":"loop_contract","support_classification":"production_supported","required_tool_capabilities":["native_loop_contract"],"candidate_statement":"A candidate loop-contract property can restate the existing CBMC loop annotations for mlk_poly_add: at loop index i, indices below i have already been updated to loop_entry(*r).coeffs[k] + b->coeffs[k], while indices from i through MLKEM_N-1 remain equal to loop_entry(*r).coeffs[k].","supporting_evidence":[{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/poly.c","locator":"mlk_poly_add loop invariants","excerpt":"invariant(forall(k0, i, MLKEM_N, r->coeffs[k0] == loop_entry(*r).coeffs[k0])) invariant(forall(k1, 0, i, r->coeffs[k1] == loop_entry(*r).coeffs[k1] + b->coeffs[k1]))","supports_claim":"The source already contains the exact prefix/suffix invariant structure needed for a loop-contract style property.","confidence":"high"},{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/cbmc.h","locator":"loop_entry and forall macros","excerpt":"#define loop_entry(...) __CPROVER_loop_entry(__VA_ARGS__)
