s too broad: local CBMC checking of one C routine cannot establish full standard compliance.","evidence_references":[{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-agent-workflow-26-property-test/inputs/specs/fips203_clean.txt","locator":"Sections 2.4.4-2.4.5","excerpt":"The algebraic operations of addition and scalar multiplication in R_q and T_q are done coordinate-wise.","supports_claim":"The spec provides algebraic semantics, but not a proof of implementation compliance.","confidence":"high"},{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/poly.h","locator":"mlk_poly_add comment","excerpt":"@spec{@[FIPS203, 2.4.5, Arithmetic With Polynomials and NTT Representations]. Used in @[FIPS203, Algorithm 14 (K-PKE.Encrypt), L21].}","supports_claim":"There is a traceability link, but not full compliance evidence.","confidence":"high"}]},{"property_id":"P16_MLK_POLY_ADD_GLOBAL_CORRECTNESS","title":"Whole-program or caller-context correctness for mlk_poly_add","reason":"Rejected/downgraded because the available evidence supports only a local function contract and not all caller contexts. Caller-side bounds are not established in the provided primary evidence.","evidence_references":[{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-repos/mlkem-native/mlkem/src/poly.h","locator":"mlk_poly_add contract","excerpt":"requires(forall(k0, 0, MLKEM_N, (int32_t) r->coeffs[k0] + b->coeffs[k0] <= INT16_MAX)) requires(forall(k1, 0, MLKEM_N, (int32_t) r->coeffs[k1] + b->coeffs[k1] >= INT16_MIN))","supports_claim":"The contract depends on caller-established bounds.","confidence":"high"},{"source_path":"/home/girish/thesis-agent-workflow-26-property-test/inputs/specs/fips203_clean.txt","locator":"Section 7.2 and 7.3","excerpt":"ML-KEM.Encaps shall not be run with an encapsulation key that has not been checked as above... ML-KEM.Decaps shall not be run with a decapsulation key or a ciphertext unless both have been checked.","supports_claim":"The spec contains upstream checked-input requirements, b